# Copy to .eif/local-denylist.txt (NOT this .example file) and fill in your
# own instance-specific sensitive strings: private repo names, customer
# names, internal hostnames, real usernames, machine paths, anything that
# would leak if it ended up in a public artifact.
#
# .eif/local-denylist.txt is gitignored by default (see .gitignore) and is
# read by scripts/eif_privacy_scan.py in addition to its built-in checks.
# One pattern per line, plain substring match (not a regex) unless noted.
#
# Example entries (replace with your own):
# my-private-repo-name
# Real Person Name
# internal-hostname.example.corp
